#
# This file intentionally contains no canonical Malbolge bytes yet. It reserves
# the guest-side module identity for version-one DOOM capability call frames.
# jig-ignore-next-line: indivisible reviewed identifier
# The future C-to-Malbolge pipeline must generate and verify this module from the
# deterministic ABI contract rather than hand-translating declarations.
#
# Runtime rule: a .malbolge capsule declaring doom.host.v1 must cause the CLI or
# runtime linker to load this module automatically. Ordinary Malbolge programs
# must not receive DOOM capabilities implicitly.
#
# Debug telemetry capability 0x0600 version 1 operation 0 accepts canonical
# length-delimited UTF-8 language, source identity, execution location, and
# active
# instruction text. A Malbolge executor reports language=MALBOLGE,
# source=<artifact>, location=<cell/address>, and the current graphical
# instruction byte so the host title can display real execution. Telemetry is
# optional observation and is omitted when capability discovery is unavailable.
#
# Relative mouse capture capability 0x0601 version 1 operation 0 carries one
# canonical byte boolean plus seven zero reserved bytes. Capture records desired
# relative-input state; focus may temporarily release native capture without
# changing the guest request.
#
# Blocked by: versioned-host-capability-call-abi, state-aware-malbolge-linker,
# cross-platform-native-capability-runners, and C-to-Malbolge code generation.
